the southern desert regional police  academy held a graduation today at the  college of southern nevada very exciting  stuff jeremy j ford attended as 12  graduates were represented by several  agencies  it's real it's not no strong park lanson  decosta is now a police officer whose  journey to becoming one started in high  school i went to high school at veterans  tribute career technical academy where i  majored in law enforcement eventually  becoming a corrections officer wanting  to change lives i worked at ndoc for two  years and i realized i wanted to do more  and help a lot of the guys that were in  there to stay out of prison decosta  decided to join the southern desert  regional police academy and along with  11 other recruits became an officer of  the law  [Applause]  [Music]  so they'll head to their prospective  agencies they will then start their  advanced academy training prior to them  going into field training where they'll  spend about four more weeks before  becoming a solo officer it's still just  the beginning so there's still going to  be a lot of like troubles to get over  but it's a nice relief to know at least  this chapter is over with as officer  andrea flinter starts her career she  offers this advice  to not categorize all the police  officers we're human it's going to be  bad people in every profession can't  judge everybody based off of one person  while on a journey to serve and protect  our city i definitely want them to fill  a purpose i want them to understand that  there's a need for them there's a desire  for them to be in this community and  that they are  supported jeremy j ford live local now
 

